description: After any git commit in this repo, always push to origin
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commit + push together

In this repository, when the user asks to commit (or when a commit is made at their request):

1. Create the commit as usual (follow existing commit message style).
2. **Always push immediately after** with `git push -u origin HEAD` (or the current tracking branch).
3. Do not stop after commit-only unless the user explicitly says **not** to push.

Report both the commit hash/message and that the push succeeded (or failed).
